{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:19465483 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:19465483 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"19465483","source":"MED","pmid":"19465483","pmcid":"PMC2742841","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC2742841"]},"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m109.013599","title":"Regulatory subunit I-controlled protein kinase A activity is required for apical bile canalicular lumen development in hepatocytes.","authorString":"Wojtal KA, Diskar M, Herberg FW, Hoekstra D, van Ijzendoorn SC.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Wojtal KA","firstName":"Kacper A","lastName":"Wojtal","initials":"KA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Cell Biology, Section of Membrane Cell Biology, University Medical Center Groningen, University of Groningen, Groningen 9713AV, The Netherlands."}]}},{"fullName":"Diskar M","firstName":"Mandy","lastName":"Diskar","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Herberg FW","firstName":"Friedrich W","lastName":"Herberg","initials":"FW","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7117-7653"}},{"fullName":"Hoekstra D","firstName":"Dick","lastName":"Hoekstra","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"van Ijzendoorn SC","firstName":"Sven C D","lastName":"van Ijzendoorn","initials":"SC"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7117-7653"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"31","volume":"284","journalIssueId":1639094,"dateOfPublication":"2009 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2009,"printPublicationDate":"2009-07-01","journal":{"title":"The Journal of biological chemistry","medlineAbbreviation":"J Biol Chem","issn":"0021-9258","nlmid":"2985121R","essn":"1083-351X","isoabbreviation":"J Biol Chem"}},"pubYear":"2009","pageInfo":"20773-20780","abstractText":"Signaling via cAMP plays an important role in apical cell surface dynamics in epithelial cells. In hepatocytes, elevated levels of cAMP as well as extracellular oncostatin M stimulate apical lumen development in a manner that depends on protein kinase A (PKA) activity. However, neither the identity of PKA isoforms involved nor the mechanisms of the cross-talk between oncostatin M and cAMP/PKA signaling pathways have been elucidated. Here we demonstrate that oncostatin M and PKA signaling converge at the level of the PKA holoenzyme downstream of oncostatin M-stimulated MAPK activation. Experiments were performed with chemically modified cAMP analogues that preferentially target regulatory subunit (R) I or RII holoenzymes, respectively, in hepatocytes. The data suggest that the dissociation of RI- but not RII-containing holoenzymes, as well as catalytic activity of PKA, is required for apical lumen development in response to elevated levels of cAMP and oncostatin M. However, oncostatin M signaling does not stimulate PKA holoenzyme dissociation in living cells. Based on pharmacological and cell biological studies, it is concluded that RI-controlled PKA activity is essential for cAMP- and oncostatin M-stimulated development of apical bile canalicular lumens.","affiliation":"Department of Cell Biology, Section of Membrane Cell Biology, University Medical Center Groningen, University of Groningen, Groningen 9713AV, The Netherlands.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Bile Canaliculi","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Line, Tumor"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Nucleus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DE"